{"id":1662159,"title":"Astral Dice","summary":"Astral Dice is a survival expansion mod built around dice. Equip a dice and every melee attack becomes a roll of fate — trigger the Dice Blessing and enter a dice-battle system where attack clashes against defense.","description":"\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eAstral Dice — a dice-driven combat expansion for Minecraft 1.21.1 (NeoForge) and 1.20.1 (Forge).\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eEquip a dice and every melee attack rolls for a \u003cstrong\u003eDice Blessing\u003c/strong\u003e: your attack roll is checked against the target's defense roll, and the winner deals the damage. Around that core sit cards, signs, chips and four player resources that all feed back into the dice battle.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003eCore features\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cul\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eDice — 13 kinds.\u003c/strong\u003e Upgrade from the Basic Dice up to the \u003cstrong\u003eNether Star Dice\u003c/strong\u003e: Golden / Glass / Netherrack → Diamond / Emerald / Obsidian / Weird / Amethyst → Netherite / Crimson / Ender → Nether Star. Star upgrades (0–3) raise the cost pool and the number of card slots (0★ = 4, 1★ = 6, 2★ = 8, 3★ = 12, split evenly between attack and defense).\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eBattle cards — 12 kinds\u003c/strong\u003e (9 attack / 3 defense). They sit in the dice card inventory, add random points during a Dice Blessing, and each carries its own durability.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eEffect cards — 17 kinds.\u003c/strong\u003e King's Power, Berserk, Unwavering, Fight Poison with Poison, Monster Laser, Monster Brick, Orbital Strike, Directional Blast, Living Page, Fate's Guidance, Barricade, Reinforced Repulsion and more. Each card tracks its own play count and cooldown cycle.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eSigns — 31 characters.\u003c/strong\u003e Every sign has one passive and one active skill: Business, Sweeper, Guardian, Ninja, Vampire, Fengshui Master, Cult Leader, Oasis Queen, Mamushi, Mechanic, Bartender, Dorothy, Sister, Big Fat Fish, KAngel, Ame and others.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eChips — 67 pieces.\u003c/strong\u003e Passive curios such as Boxing Gloves, Speed Skates, Moto Helmet, Medkit, Magic Quiver, Electric Sword, Star Coin Hammer, Cutter and Flashlight. They grant attack, defense, movement speed, health, starlight and other bonuses.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003cstrong\u003ePlayer resources.\u003c/strong\u003e Healing points, starlight, mark stacks and charge stacks — four systems that interact with signs and chips.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eCombat HUD.\u003c/strong\u003e Dedicated Attack Power and Defense bars drawn on the vanilla armor row, and Jade shows this mod's Defense value instead of vanilla armor.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ul\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003eWhat is new in 1.5.0\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cul\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eSix new signs\u003c/strong\u003e: KAngel and Ame (Bizarre quality, sharing the \"One Body, One Soul\" team note), plus Bartender, Dorothy, Sister and Big Fat Fish.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eTwo new effect cards\u003c/strong\u003e: Barricade (a 30-durability body with a fence-height collision block that pulls aggro) and Reinforced Repulsion (exclusive, 100 durability, clamps hostile targets inside an aura with Slowness and Weakness).\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eNew chips\u003c/strong\u003e: Flashlight — Burst, Fortune Stick, Reagent — Abyss, Wireless Transmission Pole and Sensor Device.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eCard Shop and Chip Shop blocks\u003c/strong\u003e, each a villager job site, so villagers can become Card Traders and Chip Traders and sell cards or chips by level.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eEvent system rewritten\u003c/strong\u003e around a unified name / icon / type / tier / scope model with per-event timers, plus twelve new events (Red-Heat Warning, Swift Stride, Storm Approaching, Learn from Others, Shop Bonanza, Hand Erasure, World Collapse, Gift from the Sky, Angel Descent, Problem Delivery, Crowded Passage, Battle Frenzy). The Strange Question Mark item and the Lottery Box block draw events on demand.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eCards are traded, not crafted\u003c/strong\u003e: the old card crafting recipes are gone; cards come from shops and traders, and exclusive / Pinnacle / Bizarre cards never enter shops or trades.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eShop rules reworked\u003c/strong\u003e: a 60-second cycle, a fresh batch only when the shelf is empty, one transfer and one starlight exchange per cycle, and reopening no longer rerolls the shelf.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eSign internals consolidated\u003c/strong\u003e (sign-hook dispatcher, shared equip checks, unified attribute and effect application, ten sign attachments merged into one), with the shared utility layer moved into the StarEngine library.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eFive new custom sound effects, the 179-sprite Iron Elden Ring particle library, and a batch of fixes (firearm damage attribution, laser and explosion damage entries, Living Page stacking, Medkit refill on relog, guidebook rarities).\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ul\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003eSupported versions\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003ctable\u003e\n\u003cthead\u003e\n\u003ctr\u003e\n\u003cth\u003eFile\u003c/th\u003e\n\u003cth\u003eMinecraft\u003c/th\u003e\n\u003cth\u003eLoader\u003c/th\u003e\n\u003cth\u003eJava\u003c/th\u003e\n\u003cth\u003eCurrent version\u003c/th\u003e\n\u003c/tr\u003e\n\u003c/thead\u003e\n\u003ctbody\u003e\n\u003ctr\u003e\n\u003ctd\u003e\u003ccode\u003eastral_dice-\u0026lt;version\u0026gt;+neoforge_1.21.1.jar\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003ctd\u003e1.21.1\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003ctd\u003eNeoForge 21.1.235+\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003ctd\u003e21\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003ctd\u003e\u003cstrong\u003e1.5.0-rc.1\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003c/tr\u003e\n\u003ctr\u003e\n\u003ctd\u003e\u003ccode\u003eastral_dice-\u0026lt;version\u0026gt;+forge_1.20.1.jar\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003ctd\u003e1.20.1\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003ctd\u003eForge 47.4.10+\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003ctd\u003e17\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003ctd\u003e\u003cstrong\u003e1.5.0-rc.1\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003c/tr\u003e\n\u003c/tbody\u003e\n\u003c/table\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eBoth builds are release lines kept at feature parity, and both jars ship with every release. These are the only published builds — there is no build for any other Minecraft version or loader.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003eRequired dependencies\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cul\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eStarEngine\u003c/strong\u003e (mod id \u003ccode\u003estarengine\u003c/code\u003e, currently \u003cstrong\u003e1.1.0\u003c/strong\u003e) — \u003cstrong\u003edownload it separately from its own CurseForge project\u003c/strong\u003e and put the matching jar (\u003ccode\u003estarengine-neoforge-1.21.1-1.1.0.jar\u003c/code\u003e / \u003ccode\u003estarengine-forge-1.20.1-1.1.0.jar\u003c/code\u003e) into your \u003ccode\u003emods\u003c/code\u003e folder next to this mod. It is \u003cstrong\u003enot\u003c/strong\u003e bundled. The accepted range is \u003ccode\u003e[1.1.0, 2.0.0)\u003c/code\u003e; a missing or older library aborts startup with \u003cem\u003eMissing or unsupported mandatory dependencies\u003c/em\u003e.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eCurios API\u003c/strong\u003e — \u003ccode\u003e9+\u003c/code\u003e on 1.21.1, \u003ccode\u003e5.x\u003c/code\u003e on 1.20.1 Forge. A missing or too-old Curios is rejected during dependency sorting.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eA Mixin runtime (1.20.1 Forge only)\u003c/strong\u003e — either \u003cstrong\u003eMixin Booster 0.1.3+\u003c/strong\u003e or \u003cstrong\u003eSinytra Connector\u003c/strong\u003e. If your pack already ships Sinytra Connector, nothing else is needed; when neither is present the mod refuses to start and explains what to install.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ul\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003eOptional\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cul\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003cstrong\u003ePatchouli\u003c/strong\u003e — the in-game guide book.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eBountiful\u003c/strong\u003e — bounty board integration.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ul\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003eInstallation\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003col\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eInstall the loader for your Minecraft version (NeoForge 21.1 for 1.21.1, Forge 47.4.10 for 1.20.1) and the required dependencies above.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eDrop the matching \u003ccode\u003eastral_dice-*.jar\u003c/code\u003e into your \u003ccode\u003emods\u003c/code\u003e folder — pick the file whose loader \u003cstrong\u003eand\u003c/strong\u003e Minecraft version match your instance, and pair it with the StarEngine jar of the same loader.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eLaunch. If a required dependency is missing or too old, the mod refuses to start and names exactly what to install.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ol\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003eLinks\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cul\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eSource \u0026 issue tracker\u003c/strong\u003e: \u003ca href=\"https://github.com/merlin-kitsune/astral_dice\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\"\u003ehttps://github.com/merlin-kitsune/astral_dice\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eReleases\u003c/strong\u003e (changelogs, both builds): \u003ca href=\"https://github.com/merlin-kitsune/astral_dice/releases\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\"\u003ehttps://github.com/merlin-kitsune/astral_dice/releases\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eStarEngine library\u003c/strong\u003e: \u003ca href=\"https://www.curseforge.com/minecraft/mc-mods/starengine\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\"\u003ehttps://www.curseforge.com/minecraft/mc-mods/starengine\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ul\u003e","game":"minecraft","type":"Mods","urls":{"curseforge":"https://www.curseforge.com/minecraft/mc-mods/astral-dice","project":"https://www.curseforge.com/minecraft/mc-mods/astral-dice"},"thumbnail":"https://media.forgecdn.net/avatars/thumbnails/1997/778/256/256/639229058297064871.png","created_at":"2026-08-21T11:40:24.257Z","downloads":{"monthly":0,"total":1343},"license":"","donate":"","categories":["Adventure and RPG"],"members":[{"title":"Owner","username":"MerlinKitsune","id":143651803}],"links":[],"files":[{"id":9402802,"url":"https://www.curseforge.com/minecraft/mc-mods/astral-dice/files/9402802","display":"Astral Dice 1.5.0 (Fabric 1.20.1)","name":"astral_dice-1.5.0-fabric_1.20.1.jar","type":"release","version":"1.20.1","filesize":2936067,"versions":["Client","Fabric","1.20.1","Server"],"downloads":8,"uploaded_at":"2026-11-02T05:11:05.037Z"},{"id":9402705,"url":"https://www.curseforge.com/minecraft/mc-mods/astral-dice/files/9402705","display":"Astral Dice 1.5.0 (NeoForge 26.1.2)","name":"astral_dice-1.5.0-neoforge_26.1.2.jar","type":"release","version":"26.1.2","filesize":2792140,"versions":["Client","NeoForge","Server","26.1.2"],"downloads":0,"uploaded_at":"2026-11-02T04:48:02.98Z"},{"id":9402506,"url":"https://www.curseforge.com/minecraft/mc-mods/astral-dice/files/9402506","display":"Astral Dice 1.5.0 (Forge 1.20.1)","name":"astral_dice-1.5.0-forge_1.20.1.jar","type":"release","version":"1.20.1","filesize":2662359,"versions":["Client","1.20.1","Forge","Server"],"downloads":0,"uploaded_at":"2026-11-02T04:04:40.003Z"},{"id":9402505,"url":"https://www.curseforge.com/minecraft/mc-mods/astral-dice/files/9402505","display":"Astral Dice 1.5.0 (NeoForge 1.21.1)","name":"astral_dice-1.5.0-neoforge_1.21.1.jar","type":"release","version":"1.21.1","filesize":2614053,"versions":["Client","1.21.1","NeoForge","Server"],"downloads":0,"uploaded_at":"2026-11-02T04:04:32.39Z"},{"id":9066054,"url":"https://www.curseforge.com/minecra